# GitHub Pages, which hosts the page, does not read this file. It sends its
# own fixed headers and ignores every rule here, so none of these reach a
# browser from GitHub alone. They are applied one of two ways instead:
#
#   1. Cloudflare in front of seat-airlines.space (DNS records proxied), with
#      a Response Header Transform Rule that sets each header below to the
#      same value. The steps are in docs/for-developers/deploying.md, under
#      "Security headers".
#   2. Moving the page to Cloudflare Pages, which reads this file as it is.
#
# Until one of those is in place, only the referrer policy is live, as a
# <meta> in index.html. This file is still the one list of what the headers
# should be: change a value here and in the Transform Rule together.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors https://x.com https://twitter.com https://mobile.twitter.com https://platform.twitter.com
  # X-Frame-Options is intentionally omitted: X Player Cards require framing.
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
